The signed fixed-width integer types Signed8.T, Signed16.T, Signed32.T
and Signed64.T (this fork; see
LLVM-IR-backend-docs/fixed-width-integer-types-plan.md).

Arithmetic stays inside the range here; p304 tests overflow.  Values
are sign-extended, comparisons and DIV/MOD are signed (DIV rounds
down, MOD takes the divisor's sign), x MOD -1 is 0 even for FIRST,
ABS works up to -LAST, and full-width multiplication is exact up to
the edges.  Constant folding must agree with run-time arithmetic.
Also: INC and DEC up to the edges with INTEGER and SignedN steps, FOR
loops to FIRST and LAST and with negative steps, subranges, packed
fields, arrays, sets, CASE, VAR parameters and VAL.  Every line of
output should be the same with every backend and at every
optimization level.
